    <string name="step_1_desc">Make sure both your Galaxy Watch and this phone are connected to the same Wi-Fi network.</string>
    <string name="step_1_tip">💡 Tip: If you are away from home, you can turn on Mobile Hotspot / Tethering on this phone and connect the watch to it.</string>
    <string name="step_1_title">Step 1: Wi-Fi Connection</string>
    <string name="step_2_desc">On your Galaxy Watch, go to Settings > Developer options > Wireless debugging and turn it ON.</string>
    <string name="step_2_dev_tip">Don\'t see Developer options?\nGo to Settings > About watch > Software info > and tap \'Software version\' 7 times consecutively.</string>
    <string name="step_2_title">Step 2: Wireless Debugging on Watch</string>
    <string name="step_3_desc">On the Wireless Debugging screen on your watch, tap \'Pair device with pairing code\'. Enter the IP, pairing port, and 6-digit code shown.</string>
    <string name="step_3_title">Step 3: Pair Watch</string>
    <string name="step_4_desc">Exit the pairing screen. Now enter the main port shown directly under \'IP address &amp; port\' on your watch.</string>
